10	# RHAISTRAT-9001 Decomposition — Surface model deployment status in the RHOAI Dashboard
11	
12	## Epic List
13	
14	| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |
15	|----|-------|------|------|----------|
16	| RHAISTRAT-9001-E001 | Surface InferenceService status (Ready / Progressing / Failed) in Dashboard model serving views | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |
17	| RHAISTRAT-9001-E002 | Deployment status detail view: condition messages and recent events | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P0 |
18	| RHAISTRAT-9001-E003 | Status-driven filtering and sorting of the deployed models list | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P2 |
19	| RHAISTRAT-9001-E004 | Document deployment status values and Failed troubleshooting | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |
20	
21	## Dependency DAG
22	
23	```mermaid
24	graph TD
25	    E001[RHAISTRAT-9001-E001]
26	    E002[RHAISTRAT-9001-E002]
27	    E003[RHAISTRAT-9001-E003]
28	    E004[RHAISTRAT-9001-E004]
29	    E001 --> E002
30	    E001 --> E003
31	    E001 --> E004
32	    E002 --> E004
33	```
34	
35	Arrows point from dependency to dependent: `E001 --> E002` means E001 must complete before E002 starts.
36	
37	## DAG Justification
38	
39	| Edge | Rule | Rationale |
40	|------|------|-----------|
41	| E001 → E002 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | The status detail view renders the condition and event data model that the status-surface epic establishes. Rule 13 does not apply (same repo, shared data surface — not a configuration reference). |
42	| E001 → E003 | Rule 12 (framework → consumer) | Filtering and sorting by status requires the status field on the deployed models list — the shared UI surface E001 introduces. |
43	| E001 → E004, E002 → E004 | Rule 11 (docs-authoring always last) | Documentation describes the delivered behavior and is technically reviewed against the implementation. |
44	
45	## Decomposition Rationale
46	
47	- **Step 0 triage — not triggered.** The strategy is not S-sized-single-team: it spans two components (Dashboard, KServe) and two teams (RHOAI Dashboard, RHOAI Serving), and includes substantive documentation authoring (HLR-5, a new troubleshooting topic — a distinct work-product stream).
48	- **Step 2 — component graph.**
