29	# Surface InferenceService deployment status in Dashboard model serving views
30	
31	## Description
32	
33	Deliver a deployment status indicator (Ready, Progressing, Failed) for every deployed model in the Dashboard's model serving views, so data scientists can tell whether a KServe InferenceService deployment is healthy without leaving the console or running `oc` commands. The status must reflect the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without a manual page reload.
34	
35	## Scope
36	
37	- Add a deployment status field (Ready / Progressing / Failed) to the deployed models list and model serving detail views in the Dashboard.
38	- Derive the displayed status from the InferenceService CR status conditions and recent Kubernetes events exposed by KServe (serving.kserve.io/v1beta1), per the Dashboard's existing pattern of reading component CRs through the Kubernetes API.
39	- Include the passive-component validation: verify the existing KServe InferenceService status conditions are sufficient to distinguish all three displayed statuses; if a state cannot be derived from existing conditions, that is a defect to resolve (fix-and-retry), not a scope change.
40	- Status refresh path so the displayed state tracks the actual InferenceService state within 30 seconds of a change, without requiring a manual page reload.
41	- Incidental updates to existing view captions or references that fall out of this change.
42	
43	## Acceptance Criteria
44	
45	- Given a deployed model whose InferenceService is Ready, When the user views the model serving list or model detail, Then a "Ready" status is displayed for that model.
46	- Given a deployment that is progressing or failed, When the user views the model serving views, Then "Progressing" or "Failed" is displayed respectively.
47	- Given a change in the InferenceService's actual state, When 30 seconds have elapsed, Then the displayed status reflects the new state without a manual page reload (HLR-3, measured by observing the UI after a state change with no reload).
48	- The status derivation for each InferenceService state (Ready, Progressing, Failed) is verified against the condition set KServe exposes on the InferenceService status; any state that cannot be represented is fixed before completion.
49	- Existing model serving views are not regressed (existing list, detail, and deployment flows still function).
50	
51	## HLR Traceability
52	
53	- HLR-1 (P0): status visible per deployed model in model serving views.
54	- HLR-3 (P1): status reflects actual state within 30 seconds, no manual reload (bundled here — same data path and views as HLR-1; splitting would duplicate the same implementation surface).
