30	# Deployment status detail view: condition messages and recent events
31	
32	## Description
33	
34	Deliver a status detail view in the Dashboard that a user can open for a failed or progressing model deployment, showing the underlying InferenceService condition messages and the recent Kubernetes events for that deployment. This turns "my model has been Pending for an hour" support cases into self-service diagnosis: the information the platform already has becomes visible in the console.
35	
36	## Scope
37	
38	- Add a status detail view (or expandable panel) reachable from the deployment status shown in the model serving views, for deployments in Failed or Progressing state.
39	- Surface the InferenceService CR status condition messages (e.g. Ready, PredictorReady conditions with reasons and messages).
40	- Surface the recent Kubernetes events associated with the deployment.
41	- Read all data through the Dashboard's existing Kubernetes API access pattern; no new private component APIs.
42	- Incidental updates to captions or references that fall out of this change.
43	
44	## Acceptance Criteria
45	
46	- Given a deployment in Failed or Progressing state, When the user opens the status detail view, Then the underlying condition messages for that InferenceService are displayed.
47	- Given a deployment with recent Kubernetes events, When the user opens the status detail view, Then those recent events are displayed (measured by comparing the view against `oc describe`/`oc get events` output for the same InferenceService).
48	- Given a deployment in Ready state, When the user views the model serving views, Then the detail view either is not offered or shows the same data consistently with the Ready status.
49	- The view renders for InferenceService deployments in both serverless and raw deployment modes (KServe InferenceService scope; ModelMesh deployments are out of scope).
50	
51	## HLR Traceability
52	
53	- HLR-2 (P0): status detail view showing condition messages and recent events for failed or progressing deployments.
